{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Extensions"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A type’s own page lists only the members of its own module. Each page here collects the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"members that every other module adds to one type."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluent\/extensions"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Grafluent"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Extensions Across Modules"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The members each module adds to types declared in another module, by extended type."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-DirectedGraph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-DirectedHypergraph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-Graph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-Hypergraph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-MutableDirectedGraph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-MutableGraph-Extensions"],"anchor":"GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule-DirectedAcyclicGraph-Extensions"],"anchor":"DirectedAcyclicGraphModule","title":"DirectedAcyclicGraphModule"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Arborescence-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-RootedTree-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Tree-Extensions"],"anchor":"Trees","title":"Trees"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/BipartiteGraphs-BipartiteGraph-Extensions"],"anchor":"BipartiteGraphs","title":"BipartiteGraphs"}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableGraph":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableGraph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableGraph"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutablegraph","abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph that generic code can fill: the undirected counterpart of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableDirectedGraph"},{"text":" (Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGraph"},{"text":" concept, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_vertex"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_edge"},{"text":"), with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"members a reader needs to build a graph by key.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"MutableGraph"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Trees-Arborescence-Extensions":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Arborescence-Extensions","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/trees-arborescence-extensions","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Members other modules add to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Extensions to Arborescence"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and no type is both. "},{"code":"directed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Graph","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods: Boost’s "},{"code":"BidirectionalGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Kept apart"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" because in-adjacency usually costs extra storage, and many algorithms only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"go forward."}],"title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedHypergraph":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedHypergraph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedHypergraph"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedhypergraph","abstract":[{"text":"A directed hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ordered pair of vertex sets, its sources (tail) and its targets (head). Gallo, Longo, Pallottino","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and Nguyen, “Directed hypergraphs and applications”, ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Discrete Applied Mathematics","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"42(2–3):177–201, 1993, define a hyperarc as “an ordered pair … of (possibly empty) disjoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subsets”; here either side may be empty and a vertex may be on both, the hypergraph form of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop (XGI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiHypergraph"},{"text":" allows both).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"DirectedHypergraph"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-DirectedHypergraph-Extensions":{"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-DirectedHypergraph-Extensions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","title":"Extensions to DirectedHypergraph","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-directedhypergraph-extensions"},"doc://DirectedAcyclicGraphModule/documentation/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule/DirectedAcyclicGraph":{"url":"\/documentation\/directedacyclicgraphmodule\/directedacyclicgraph","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/documentation\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/DirectedAcyclicGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph with no directed cycle, which keeps a topological order of its vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"current as it changes (JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", petgraph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"acyclic::Acyclic"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","type":"topic"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-MutableDirectedGraph-Extensions":{"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-MutableDirectedGraph-Extensions","abstract":[{"text":"Members other modules add to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","title":"Extensions to MutableDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-mutabledirectedgraph-extensions"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Hypergraph":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/hypergraph","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set of vertices of any size, the empty set included (Berge, "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hypergraphs"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", 1989). Not a "},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and no shared parent with one: a hyperedge is not an edge. The "},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" module’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"incidenceGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads a hypergraph as its bipartite incidence graph (the Levi graph), which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"how the graph algorithms reach it."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Hypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Hypergraph","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DirectedGraph","type":"topic"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-MutableGraph-Extensions":{"role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-MutableGraph-Extensions","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-mutablegraph-extensions","abstract":[{"text":"Members other modules add to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableGraph","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Extensions to MutableGraph"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-DirectedGraph-Extensions":{"role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-DirectedGraph-Extensions","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-directedgraph-extensions","abstract":[{"text":"Members other modules add to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Extensions to DirectedGraph"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Trees-Tree-Extensions":{"kind":"article","title":"Extensions to Tree","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Tree-Extensions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/trees-tree-extensions","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Tree":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Tree"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Tree"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/tree","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A tree: a connected, acyclic undirected graph with at least one vertex, so it has exactly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"n − 1 edges, no self-loop and no parallel edges. The invariant is the type: every initializer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from unchecked input is failable, and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot be mutated.","type":"text"}],"title":"Tree"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Arborescence":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Arborescence"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Arborescence"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/arborescence","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An arborescence: a directed tree whose edges all point away from its root, so every vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but the root has exactly one incoming edge, from its parent (NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Edmonds). A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the children, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parent (zero or one), and each edge is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedEdge(from: parent, to: child)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"Arborescence"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate: Boost’s "},{"code":"MutableGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" concept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"add_vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"add_edge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"remove_edge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"remove_vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), for a directed representation. It exists so that a wrapper which adds a rule, such as "},{"code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can own any of the mutable representations as its base and still run at the base’s speed."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"title":"MutableDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic, high-performance graph library for Swift."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Grafluent"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-Graph-Extensions":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-graph-extensions","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-Graph-Extensions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","title":"Extensions to Graph","type":"topic"},"doc://BipartiteGraphs/documentation/BipartiteGraphs/BipartiteGraph":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BipartiteGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BipartiteGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/BipartiteGraphs\/documentation\/BipartiteGraphs\/BipartiteGraph","url":"\/documentation\/bipartitegraphs\/bipartitegraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph with two fixed sides, every edge joining a left vertex to a right vertex, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no self-loop. Simple: an edge is inserted once, in either orientation. Each edge is stored left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"endpoint first, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[e].u"},{"type":"text","text":" is its left end."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"BipartiteGraph"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule-DirectedAcyclicGraph-Extensions":{"kind":"article","title":"Extensions to DirectedAcyclicGraph","abstract":[{"text":"Members other modules add to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/documentation\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/DirectedAcyclicGraph","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule-DirectedAcyclicGraph-Extensions","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/directedacyclicgraphmodule-directedacyclicgraph-extensions","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-Hypergraph-Extensions":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-hypergraph-extensions","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-Hypergraph-Extensions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","title":"Extensions to Hypergraph","type":"topic"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Trees-RootedTree-Extensions":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-RootedTree-Extensions","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/trees-rootedtree-extensions","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/RootedTree","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"Extensions to RootedTree"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/RootedTree":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/RootedTree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/rootedtree","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree with a root: an undirected "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parent(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"depth(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and the queries tree algorithms start from. The vertices, edges and their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions are the tree’s; the root orders "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (each vertex’s incident edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position order, without the edge to its parent) and so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preorder"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"RootedTree"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Extensions":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-bidirectionaldirectedgraph-extensions","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Extensions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","title":"Extensions to BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"topic"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/BipartiteGraphs-BipartiteGraph-Extensions":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/BipartiteGraphs-BipartiteGraph-Extensions","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/bipartitegraphs-bipartitegraph-extensions","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/BipartiteGraphs\/documentation\/BipartiteGraphs\/BipartiteGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"Extensions to BipartiteGraph"}}}